    "summary": "Docker containers and virtual machines both isolate applications but differ fundamentally in architecture: VMs virtualize hardware and run a full OS per instance, while containers share the host OS kernel for lightweight, fast, and portable workloads. The right choice depends on isolation needs, OS…",
